    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Expression-of-Interest---Teaching-Associate--School-of-Computing_R000023452": {
      "title": "Expression of Interest – Teaching Associate, School of Computing",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-05-28\nPart time\n\nPRIMARY DETAIL DISCOVER, CREATE, INNOVATE  The Faculty of Science and Engineering at Macquarie University delivers quality education to enable our students to reach their full potential, and work with our communities to discover, create and innovate with sustainability at our core.   THE ROLE  The School of Computing is inviting expressions of interest for inclusion within our casual academic pool for 2026.   For your application to be considered for Session 2 2026, please register your Expression of Interest (EOI) by Friday 12th June 2026 by uploading your relevant qualifications and requested details via the Workday application process. The School of Computing offers a range of undergraduate and postgraduate units to students completing courses in the Faculty of Science and Engineering, as well as service and elective units to students from across the campus. We employ casual academic staff to support our teaching of these courses.   We are currently inviting Expressions of interest (EOIs) from appropriately qualified individuals who demonstrate the following skills, qualifications, and experience.   ESSENTIAL CRITERIA   Completed Bachelor and/or Master’s degree in Computing, or a closely related discipline.  Sufficient discipline-specific knowledge  An understanding and appreciation of scholarly teaching  Excellent communication skills  Proven ability to interact effectively with students, staff and the community     TO APPLY  All interested applicants are required to upload a copy of their CV , copy of degree / testamur and a cover letter addressing the above criteria as part of the EOI process.  To assist in the review process, please complete this survey Qualtrics Survey | Qualtrics Experience Management (this survey is compulsory)   After initial review, applicants will be asked to prepare a short video to demonstrate their teaching style. If you are already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health): Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs.  If you are NOT currently part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health): click the 'Apply' button.  *Please note that this position is not available for visa sponsorship and the successful applicant must have work rights in Australia*   Position Enquiries: Elizabeth Bignucolo, Sessional Academic Staff Coordinator  at elizabeth.bignucolo@mq.edu.au Applications Close: Thursday, 31st of December 2026 11:59 pm (AEST) We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 31/12/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Lecturer-in-Engineering--Research-and-Teaching-_R000024191": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Engineering (Research and Teaching)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-11\nFull time\n\n- Salary package:  $127,138 - $150,425 (Level B.1 – B.6) plus 17% employer's superannuation contribution and annual leave loading. - Three full-time, continuing roles - Based at Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde The School of Engineering is seeking three dynamic, early-to-mid-career rising stars to join us as Lecturers (Level B) . We have the flexibility to appoint across Civil, Mechanical and Mechatronic Engineering.  We are looking for outstanding academics who bridge the gap between engineering theory and practical execution. While academic rigor is essential, we are explicitly looking for individuals who know how to build engineering artifacts. You possess strong practical engineering skills, a passion for prototyping, design, or implementation, and the ability to inspire students through hands-on, project-based education. In these roles, you will contribute to our rapidly growing undergraduate and postgraduate programs, supervise Higher Degree by Research (HDR) students, and develop an impactful, independent research profile that translates innovative ideas into tangible, real-world solutions. These roles are full-time, continuing (tenure-track) positions, based at our Wallumattagal (North Ryde) Campus in Sydney. About Us The School of Engineering at Macquarie University is rapidly expanding the capacity and impact of its research and education frameworks. As a comprehensive school, our expertise spans civil, environmental, mechanical, mechatronic, biomedical, electrical, and electronic engineering. This year, we established our operations in a brand-new, $150 million education and research precinct: the Engineering Innovation Building. This facility features state-of-the-art spaces designed specifically for immersive, team-based design and manufacturing projects, alongside specialist laboratories hosting our highly ranked research groups. As part of the Faculty of Science and Engineering (FSE), we nurture the next generation of technology innovators, supporting nearly 9,000 students across our programs. Our research and teaching directly address the critical challenges faced by global society—including infrastructure resilience, autonomous systems, future materials, and sustainable energy. To Apply To be considered for this position, candidates must submit a copy of their curriculum vitae alongside a statement of no more than five pages addressing the selection criteria outlined below. Essential criteria (Lecturer Level B) To be successful, candidates will need to demonstrate their capability across the following areas: A PhD in Civil, Mechanical, Mechatronic, or a closely related engineering discipline. Demonstrated hands-on engineering skills with a track record of physical prototyping, experimental system design, field testing, or practical project execution. Evidence of capability to design and deliver engaging, high-quality, project-led learning experiences that develop both the technical and practical competencies of engineering students. A developing or established track record of quality publications and a clear trajectory for securing external research funding or industry partnerships. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to collaborate effectively across disciplinary boundaries and work with industry partners. The Faculty of Science and Engineering at Macquarie University has a goal to increase the engagement of women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people from diverse backgrounds in STEMM roles. Applications are considered holistically, and candidates are encouraged to apply even if their experience does not meet each individual selection criterion. *This position requires a criminal history and qualifications check. Applications Close: Sunday 18th of October at 11:59pm (AEST). We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date. For enquiries, or a confidential conversation about the role please contact Professor Gordon Wyeth, Dean of School of Engineering: fse.eng-dean@mq.edu.au . Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for.  Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 18/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Associate-Professor-of-Engineering_R000024150": {
      "title": "Associate Professor of Engineering",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-11\nFull time\n\n- Salary package:  $186,433 - $205,067 (Level D.1 – D.4) plus 17% employer's superannuation contribution and annual leave loading. - Full-time, continuing role - Based at Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde About the Role The School of Engineering invites applications for an Associate Professor in Civil Engineering (Teaching and Research) with a specialization in Transport Engineering . In this role, you will deliver high-quality undergraduate and postgraduate education, supervise Higher Degree by Research (HDR) students, secure competitive research funding, and strengthen Macquarie University’s strategic connections within the transport industry. The successful applicant will have a proven track record of creating engaging learning experiences for students and driving real-world impact through their research. We are seeking candidates with expertise in making transportation systems efficient, reliable, affordable, and sustainable. Areas of particular interest include network planning and modelling, safety, public transport analysis, and environmental modelling. This is a full-time, continuing (tenure-track) position based at our Wallumattagal (North Ryde) Campus in Sydney. About Us The School of Engineering at Macquarie University is rapidly expanding the capacity and impact of its research and education frameworks. As a comprehensive school, our expertise spans civil, environmental, mechanical, mechatronic, biomedical, electrical, and electronic engineering. This year, we established our operations in a brand-new, $150 million education and research precinct: the Engineering Innovation Building. This facility features state-of-the-art spaces designed specifically for project- and team-based learning, alongside specialist laboratories hosting our highly ranked research groups. As part of the Faculty of Science and Engineering (FSE), we nurture the next generation of technology innovators, supporting nearly 9,000 students across our programs. Our research and teaching directly address the critical challenges faced by global society—including the changing environment, future materials, sustainable fuels, and biotechnology. To Apply To be considered for this position, candidates must submit a copy of their curriculum vitae alongside a statement of no more than five pages addressing the selection criteria outlined below. Essential criteria for appointment at Associate Professor (Level D) A PhD in Civil Engineering, Transport Engineering, or a closely related discipline. A demonstrated and growing national and international reputation for academic excellence, evidenced by independent, innovative, and sustained contributions to research and education in transport engineering. Demonstrated ability to lead, design, and deliver high-quality curriculum and transformative teaching and learning experiences, with a track record of high student satisfaction and engagement. Proven leadership in securing and managing competitive research grants (e.g., ARC) and/or industry-funded projects, leading to high-impact publications and tangible socio-economic or policy outcomes. A sustained track record of successful Higher Degree Research (HDR) supervision to completion, and a commitment to mentoring candidates toward successful academic or industry careers. Demonstrated leadership in contributing to a positive, collaborative, and inclusive workplace culture that values diversity of thought, equity, and the professional development of colleagues. Outstanding communication, negotiation, and interpersonal skills, with a proven ability to build strategic partnerships and work effectively with internal institutional stakeholders and external industry or government partners. The Faculty of Science and Engineering at Macquarie University has a goal to increase the engagement of women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people from diverse backgrounds in STEMM roles. Applications are considered holistically, and candidates are encouraged to apply even if their experience does not meet each individual selection criterion. *This position requires a criminal history and qualifications check. Applications Close: Sunday 18th of October 2026 at 11:59pm (AEST). We welcome applications from international candidates. We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date. For enquiries, or a confidential conversation about the role please contact Professor Gordon Wyeth, Dean of School of Engineering: fse.eng-dean@mq.edu.au Pre-Employment Checks  Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for.  Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University.  If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 18/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Manager-Collection-Services_R000024589": {
      "title": "Manager Collection Services",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-23\nFull time\n\n• Annual base salary from $126,306 - $140,543 per annum (HEW Level 8) plus 17% superannuation and annual leave loading • Full-time, continuing appointment • Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde As Manager, Collection Services, you will lead and develop the Collections Services team to deliver equitable, streamlined access to library resources, with a particular focus on prescribed learning resources that enable student success. About the Role  You will oversee core services including resource procurement, interlibrary loans and resource sharing, unit readings, accessibility services, and open educational resources, while developing the standards, documentation, and procedures that support consistent, scalable service delivery.  You will work closely with the Library Management Team to deliver on Waranara Library’s Strategic Plan 2025-2029. Reporting to the Director, Resources and Discovery, you will translate Library and University strategy into prioritised plans, service roadmaps, and measurable outcomes that improve library services and the client experience.  Your responsibilities will include:  Lead the Collections Services team to deliver equitable, timely access to prescribed and other learning resources  Provide strong people leadership through clear expectations, coaching, performance development, and workforce planning to build a high-performing team Ensure excellent end-to-end delivery of interlibrary loans and resource sharing, unit readings, accessibility services, open educational resources, and procurement  Partner with academic and professional stakeholders to understand needs, manage expectations, and improve staff and student experience Drive continuous improvement using data and feedback (including service standards, KPIs, and turnaround times), and report recommendations and risks to library management Maintain fit-for-purpose procedures, process controls, and documentation to support consistent service delivery Ensure compliance and risk management across the portfolio (including copyright and licensing, privacy/confidentiality, WHS and EEO)  Manage vendor and licence relationships to ensure value, quality, and continuity of service   About Us  The University Library provides high-quality, client-centred services, information resources and learning spaces that underpin world-class research and transformative education. In partnership with academics and other university service providers, the Library contributes to the development of graduate capabilities, research capacity, student experience, teaching excellence and community engagement About You  You are a values-led leader who cares about equitable access to information and enjoys improving services that make a genuine difference for students and staff. You bring significant leadership experience and a demonstrated ability to lead innovative, high-performing teams, along with strong stakeholder management skills and a practical approach to continuous service improvement.  Selection Criteria  Degree in an information management related discipline, with extensive management experience, or an equivalent combination of relevant experience, and qualifications/training.    Significant leadership experience with demonstrated ability to lead innovative, high-performing teams.  Extensive experience designing workflows, procedures, and implementing continuous improvement particularly in interlibrary loans, procurement, accessibility services, open educational resources, and unit readings management.   Extensive experience in integrated library management systems and specialist technologies supporting interlibrary loans and unit readings such as Alma, Leganto, Rapido, RapidILL.    Demonstrated experience developing and managing stakeholder and partner relationships.   High-level knowledge of copyright, licensing and intellectual property requirements relevant to resource acquisitions, interlibrary loans, accessibility services, open educational resources, and unit readings management, and demonstrated ability to apply this in practice.  Experience developing and implementing service delivery plans, programs and initiatives and proven ability to analyse and interpret highly complex information from numerous sources.   Other Specific Requirements:   Work hours may vary from time to time to accommodate business needs  How to Apply   To be considered, please apply online with your CV and a cover letter outlining how your experience aligns with the selection criteria (above).  Applications Close:   8 October 2026 We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date.   For a confidential conversation about the role please contact Katie Leach, Director Resources and Discovery at katie.leach@mq.edu.au .   Why Join Us?   Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Since our foundation over 60 years ago, we have aspired to be a different type of university. Over the years, we have grown to become the centre of a vibrant local and global community. Connect with us today .  We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index. Explore the fantastic benefits available to you when you become part of the team at Macquarie University.  Flexible, hybrid work arrangements  17% Superannuation  Subsidised onsite parking options  Extensive training and professional development programs  Onsite childcare facilities to support working parents  Onsite vacation care during school holidays  Discounted health insurance  Subsidised membership at our Sport & Aquatic Centre  Access to an Employee Assistance Program for free and confidential support  Convenient onsite GP, imaging, and physiotherapy clinics  Pre-Employment Checks   Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University.  If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 08/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Teacher--Diploma-of-Health-Sciences_R000024597": {
      "title": "Teacher, Diploma of Health Sciences",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-24\nFull time\n\n- Salary Package: $85,840 - $120,892 p.a., plus 17% employer's superannuation and annual leave loading - Appointment Type: Full-Time (35 hours per week), continuing appointment - Location: Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus (North Ryde) THE ROLE Macquarie University College is seeking to appoint a qualified and highly experienced Diploma of Health Sciences Teacher. This is an exciting opportunity for an enthusiastic teacher to enhance and extend education excellence at Macquarie University College. Key responsibilities include but are not limited to: Contributing to ongoing curriculum development and improvement of delivery of the College units and courses, Delivering lessons and workshops, Coordinating the teaching teams, Preparing and revising learning and teaching resources, Producing high-quality assessment tasks, Administration, supervision and marking of assessments, and participation in assessment task moderation and quality assurance processes, Consultation with students and provision of academic advice & support if needed, Consistently monitoring student progress; identifying and following up with students at risk, Contributing to the effective operations of the Macquarie University Learning Management System (iLearn) as required, Engaging professionally with colleagues and students and contribute to a positive workplace culture, Complying with relevant EEO and WHS regulations.   *** Please note the expectation is that staff will be on campus most workdays. ABOUT US Macquarie University College provides local and international students with alternative pathway programs to undergraduate and postgraduate degrees through our accelerated face-to-face learning model. The College delivers Foundation & Intensive programs, Diplomas, UniReady and Masters Qualifying programs, English language programs, and operates the Pearson Testing Centre on campus.   ABOUT YOU We are seeking a passionate, highly skilled teacher with extensive teaching experience at higher education level in a Health-related discipline to join Macquarie University College . You will have knowledge of the latest developments in learning principles including online and blended learning pedagogies and proven experience in curriculum and assessment design. Your ability to work in a fast paced and vibrant environment and a “students first” mindset will ensure your success in this role.   To Apply To be considered for this position, please apply online and attach your resume and a separate cover letter (no more than 2 pages) that outlines how you meet the selection criteria below: Essential Selection Criteria An undergraduate qualification in Health Sciences or a health-related discipline. Additional undergraduate or postgraduate qualifications, particularly in Teaching/Education would be an advantage. At least two years' experience teaching at an Australian higher education institution, ideally in a university college pathway context. Extensive experience in curriculum and assessment design, including related quality assurance processes. Extensive experience in administration of a unit of study or program as a subject lead, convenor or similar, with a demonstrated ability to coordinate and provide guidance to teaching teams. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to consult and liaise with a diverse range of stakeholders, such as students, teaching & professional staﬀ, and the management team. Strong computer skills in Microsoft Office applications, an understanding of Learning Management Systems, such as Moodle, and demonstrated integration of a range of learning technologies into a course or curriculum. An ability to work independently and collaboratively.   Note: This position is not available for visa sponsorship, and the successful applicant must have valid work rights in Australia. ***This role requires a Criminal History/Police Check Clearance and applicants are preferred to hold a current Working with Children Check (WWCC) or be willing to obtain one.   Specific Role Enquiries: Please contact Akina Banh, Administration Officer ( akina.banh@mq.edu.au ). Application Close: Sunday, 18 October 2026 at 11:59 p.m. (AEDT) Interviews are expected to be conducted face-to-face on Friday, 30 October 2026. Please ensure you are available on this day.   Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University.   If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 18/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
