    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Member-Experience-Officer_R000024201": {
      "title": "Member Experience Officer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nPart time\n\nAn exciting and fast-paced customer service role based in a busy gym that contributes to a great experience for our members. Our Member Experience team is a key function within our centre. As one of our Member Experience Officers you will be: Providing a consistent and high level of service to members and guests to drive acquisition and member retention. Responding to and actioning customer queries in-person, over the phone and via email. Executing acquisition and retention strategies and campaigns to sell memberships. Following established processes and procedures for memberships, point of sale transactions, cash handling, end-to-end venue hire bookings, and administration processes associated with the Centres operations and safety policy. Respond to member and guest feedback, providing constructive information to continuously improve outcomes that support a positive customer experience. About You To be successful in this role you will need: Proven experience in a front-line customer facing role. Demonstrated success in achieving sales targets, prioritising tasks, and meeting deadlines. A proven record of accomplishment in the area of customer experience and continuous improvement. Well-developed interpersonal and communication skills including the ability to work collaboratively and to establish, build and maintain respectful and ethical relationships with staff, students, and other key stakeholders. Excellent organisational and time management skills and attention to detail. Proficient skills in Microsoft Office applications, including database management. This role requires a criminal history check, First Aid and CPR certificate. Standard work hours will require you to be available on weekends, early mornings and evenings to meet the needs of the business. About Us Macquarie University Sport and Aquatic Centre (MUSAC) is a multi-purpose venue designed to help meet all the health, fitness and sporting needs of our members and guests. Our facilities include a 6-lane heated indoor pool, and an 8-lane outdoor heated Olympic-sized swimming pool. The centre features a fully equipped health club, group and virtual fitness classes, squash courts, gymnastics / aquatics programs and social sports. Macquarie University Sport Fields operates 7 days a week, our facilities include 5 professional playing fields which accommodates a variety of events, stadium lighting, canteen and BBQ areas, and four change rooms. Benefits: Complementary Macquarie University Sport & Aquatic Centre gym access Access to our staff wellbeing program and staff support services  Working on a vibrant parkland campus, with a huge variety of food & beverage outlets, and general practice & hospital amenities Access to discounted corporate health insurance and employee flu shot program Staff discounts at Campus Life operated hospitality outlets To Apply: If being part of an inclusive, vibrant, team orientated organisation is something you are passionate about we encourage you to apply.   In the first instance, general enquiries should be directed to Xavier Maniacara on 02 9850 1022, or via email xavier.maniacara@mq.edu.au . To be considered for this position, you must submit your CV and a cover letter addressing the listed criteria in the About You section via our online application portal. If you need any support or reasonable adjustments through this recruitment process, please let us know so we can provide the support you need. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 19/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Knowledge-Specialist_R000024742": {
      "title": "Knowledge Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nPart time\n\n- Casual opportunity - Service Improvement Program - $74.36 per hour (HEW 8) + 25% casual loading + 12% super - Enjoy a vibrant on-campus location, close to public transport Shape how research knowledge is captured, curated and reused – and see your work applied at scale In this role, you will design the knowledge environment for Macquarie University's Research Program – the frameworks, taxonomies, repositories, and content that make evidence, methodologies and lessons learned genuinely accessible to researchers, professional staff, industry and community partners. Reporting to the Research Program Manager within Service Improvement, you will work across a program that brings diverse expertise into one place. If you enjoy moving between design and practical delivery – this role offers real scope to make a difference. About the Role As Knowledge Specialist – Research Program, you will: Develop and implement the Research Program Knowledge Management Plan Build and maintain SharePoint knowledge repositories, knowledge bases, FAQs, templates and guidance materials Draft, edit, curate and publish knowledge articles, research insights, lessons learned, methodologies and research resources Gather content from researchers and subject matter experts, translating complex information into accessible, plain-language content Maintain knowledge article trackers and publication schedules, and monitor milestones, risks, issues and deliverables against knowledge management plans Conduct content reviews and audits so that knowledge assets remain current, accurate and useful Test and refine search functionality (AI), keywords, and user experience Facilitate workshops and stakeholder engagement meetings, as required Provide training to lift knowledge management capability across the program Advance continuous improvement and wider adoption of knowledge management practice About Us Service Improvement partners across the University to deliver programs that change how our people work. The Research Program brings together researchers and professional staff to generate, translate and apply knowledge – and this role makes certain that knowledge endures well beyond any single project. About You You are an experienced knowledge or information management practitioner who is as comfortable analysing content and building knowledge capability. You translate complexity into clarity, you know your way around SharePoint, and you build credibility quickly with researchers and senior stakeholders in busy, evolving environments. Selection Criteria Tertiary qualifications in Information Management, Research Management, or a related discipline, with equivalent experience also considered Demonstrated hands-on capability with SharePoint, knowledge bases, and content management systems, including search optimisation and user experience testing Proven track record creating, editing, and publishing knowledge articles, guidance materials and templates for varied audiences Experience working with subject matter experts and stakeholders in complex or matrixed environments Well-developed reporting, project coordination, and stakeholder engagement capability, including preparation of papers for governance forums Capacity to combine plan with day-to-day operational delivery, alongside experience facilitating workshops, training, or communities of practice How to Apply To be considered, please apply online with your CV and a cover letter outlining how your experience aligns with the selection criteria (above). Applications Close: 11:59pm AEDT, 30 October 2026 We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date. For enquiries, or a confidential conversation about the role please contact Swati Srivastava, Head of Commercial at swati.srivastava@mq.edu.au Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. If you are already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you will need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 30/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/English-for-Academic-Purposes-Teachers_R000024774-1": {
      "title": "English for Academic Purposes Teachers",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nPart time\n\nExpressions of interest are invited for casual teaching opportunities in English for Academic Purposes programs at Macquarie University College. The Role Macquarie University College  within Macquarie University, is currently inviting expressions of interest from appropriately qualified and experienced teachers for our English Language Intensive Courses for Overseas Students (ELICOS) programs. As a teacher with us, you are expected to: ·       be up to date with contemporary teaching methodology to prepare and deliver EAP lessons, ·       mark assessments and provide targeted, meaningful feedback ·       undertake student consultation, ·       work collaboratively with staff and students, ·       supervise in-class assessments and examinations, ·       manage and submit results, and ·       closely monitor and report on student progress and attendance About Us Macquarie University College provides local and international students with an alternative pathway to the University’s undergraduate degree offerings, and the English Language Program prepares international students for university study through the delivery of English language and academic literacy programs. About You You are a dedicated teaching professional with qualifications and experience in English language teaching. You have the expertise and enthusiasm to motivate and educate students in a high-stakes EAP program. Selection Criteria Qualified English Language teacher with a minimum of: ·       A recognised 3-year degree or equivalent; and ·       A recognised pre-service TESOL certificate with practicum component of no less than 6 hours supervised practice; and ·       Up to and including 3 years full-time English for Academic Purposes teaching experience ·       The ability to operate and adapt in a fast-paced environment ·       Preparedness to work collaboratively with staff and students ·       Good administrative skills and attention to detail   Desired Criteria ·       Master of Applied Linguistics/TESOL/Education or equivalent ·       IELTS or Cambridge examiner experience Successful Expressions of Interest will be kept on file and may be considered by the College when a vacancy arises that is an appropriate match to their skill base, disciplinary background and availability. *** Neither having an Expression of Interest on file nor being considered for a vacancy imply that employment is guaranteed. Please note that by providing an Expression of Interest for these positions, you agree that your details may be placed on file for a period of 24 months.  To Apply To be considered for this position, please apply online and attach your resume and a separate cover letter no more than 2 pages that outlines how you meet the selection criteria. Enquiries: For role related enquiries, please contact Cara Dinneen at  cara.dinneen@mq.edu.au Application Closing Date : Sunday 25 October 2026 at 11:59 PM (AEDT).    If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 24/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Finance-Business-Partner_R000024808-1": {
      "title": "Finance Business Partner",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nTo provide a high level of executive support and management of financial performance to Macquarie University Health. Competitive annual package circa $172K (including superannuation) Full-time, continuing contract Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde   Financial expertise meets strategic impact in Australia’s only integrated academic Health precinct. About the role   We are seeking an experienced Finance Business Partner to join our Macquarie University Health finance team, where you’ll play a pivotal role in shaping the financial performance and future success of Macquarie University Hospital and Health Clinics (MQ Health).   As a Finance Business Partner, you will work as a trusted advisor, partnering closely with senior stakeholders to provide critical financial insights and drive business decision-making. This is an opportunity to combine your financial expertise with your leadership and strategic capabilities to make a meaningful impact across a unique healthcare operation.   The Finance Business Partner works at the intersection of finance and strategy, translating complex data into actionable intelligence that drives business outcomes. This is a high impact role where you will partner directly with the Hospital Leadership and senior Health Finance and Commercial Managers in supporting desired strategic outcomes.   What will you do   Partner strategically with key stakeholders to understand their business needs and provide expert financial guidance that influences direction and decision-making. Drive business performance through insightful analysis, scenario modelling, and cost-benefit evaluations that support new initiatives and strategic imperatives. Lead continuous improvement activities within business units, that embed efficient finance processes. Shape financial planning by partnering with business units to develop and critically evaluate annual budgets, forecasts, and long-term financial plans. Deliver high-impact analysis and insights through month-end analyses and management information that tell the story behind the numbers.   About You: (Selection Criteria)   You have experience as a Finance Business Partner managing multiple stakeholders ideally within a large and complex healthcare (or similar) environment. With business partnering expertise, sound knowledge of commercial finance and the external finance landscape, you can apply this knowledge to support and influence stakeholders across all levels to ensure delivery. In addition, you will have the following:   Professional credentials – CA/CPA or equivalent qualification. Substantial experience – At least 4 years post CA/CPA experience in similar roles within large, complex organisations. Business partnering excellence – Proven ability to build rapport and influence senior stakeholders with trust and credibility. Financial Modelling – including scenario analysis and presenting actionable insights to support strategy and decision making. Commercial acumen – Sharp business insight combined with experience applying strong accounting principles. Advanced technical skills – Expertise in financial modelling, scenario analysis, and Microsoft Office (particularly Excel and PowerPoint).   Experience as a Finance Business Partner in the hospital, healthcare or similar sector is highly advantageous.   Why work at Macquarie     Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Celebrating its 60th year in 2024, it was established as a bold experiment in higher education and designed to break from educational traditions to work in tandem with industry. Institutionally we strive for the extraordinary by challenging convention and embracing different views. Our pioneering culture has encouraged and inspired students, staff and collaborators to break free from conventional thinking, and to actively shape the complex issues that define the future of humanity Connect with us today .    MQ Health Finance is a stand-alone finance function for Macquarie University Health.  It provides dedicated end-to-end Financial Performance and Business Partnering and support within the matrix structure of the broader Group Finance organization.  This stand-alone approach reflects the importance of MQ Health to the University Group, as its largest controlled entity with turnover in excess of $200M – approx. 20% of total Group revenues.  MQ Health has also recently made a step change in profitability, lifting from a historical break-even baseline to a sustained outlook for $15M+ in Operating Cash (EBITDA) each year.   Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity.  Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for.   Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University.   How to apply   Please apply online and attach your resume and a separate cover letter that outlines how your experience is aligned to the role against the selection criteria.   *Please note this position requires criminal record check.   Applications Close:   Sunday 25 October at 11:59pm AEDT   We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date.  If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 25/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Financial-Planning-and-Analysis-Analyst_R000024784-1": {
      "title": "Financial Planning and Analysis Analyst",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nTo support financial planning, management reporting and analysis across Macquarie University Health including providing support to senior members in the Finance Planning and Analysis team. Base salary from $114,992 - $124,676 (HEW Level 7), plus 17% superannuation Full-time continuing role Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde   About the role We’re looking for a commercially minded and analytically driven Financial Planning & Analysis (FP&A) Analyst to join our high performing finance team at Macquarie University Health . This role offers the opportunity to work across a diverse healthcare enterprise, providing financial insights, forecasting and performance analysis that support operational and strategic decision making. Working closely with Finance colleagues and operational stakeholders, you will contribute to financial planning, performance reporting and business analysis while supporting improvements in financial systems, processes and reporting capabilities for Macquarie University Health. What you will do Analyse financial and operational performance, including revenue, expenditure, workforce and activity trends, to identify key drivers, risks and opportunities. Prepare monthly and quarterly management reports, providing meaningful analysis and commentary on financial performance. Develop budget templates, forecasts and long-term financial plans for Macquarie University Health, including capital projections, assumption validation and system uploads. Support the preparation of detailed 5-year budgets (including capital) for senior Finance stakeholders. Build financial models, evaluations and cost-benefit analyses to support business cases, service planning and operational improvements. Support the enhancement of reporting, planning and business intelligence systems, collaborating with IT to improve data quality, automation and workflows Build and maintain stakeholder relationships across Finance and the broader business, addressing financial enquiries and coordinating with operational managers About Us Macquarie University Health is Macquarie University's integrated health and medical enterprise, encompassing Macquarie University Hospital, medical imaging, mental health services (Mindspot) and a network of more than 20 specialist clinics. As the University's largest controlled entity, it generates annual turnover in excess of $200 million. Given the scale, complexity and commercial nature of Macquarie University Health's operations, it is supported by a dedicated Finance function that provides end-to-end financial performance management and business partnering. Operating within the broader Macquarie University Group Finance structure, Macquarie University Health Finance serves as a critical enabler of informed decision-making across a uniquely diverse and fast-growing health enterprise. About you (Selection Criteria) You have expertise in conducting research and analysis with a commercial focus, within a large organisation with complex accounting and reporting requirements. Experience in FP&A in a healthcare context would be an advantage. You are an excellent communicator, and thrive in fast-paced, dynamic environments. You build and maintain good, respectful relationships with a diverse range of stakeholders, consistently demonstrating professionalism and a collaborative mindset to achieve shared outcomes. Tertiary qualification in Accounting, Finance or a related discipline. Relevant experience in accounting, finance, or equivalent. Proven ability to build and apply financial models and conduct scenario analyses. Strong experience in forecasting financials, budget preparation and financial modelling to produce business models. Strong analytical skills with the ability to manipulate and interpret large volumes of financial and operational data, identify material issues and communicate findings clearly. Business Intelligence systems and reporting platforms skills e.g. PowerBI, Tableau, Cognos TM1, Calumo. Advanced Microsoft Office skills (particularly Excel and PowerPoint). Strong experience working with large Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP) systems (preferably FinanceOne). *Please note this role requires a criminal record check. How to Apply To be considered, please apply online with your CV and a cover letter outlining how your experience aligns with the selection criteria (above). Applications Close: 25 October 2026 We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date. Why Join Us? Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Since our foundation over 60 years ago, we have aspired to be a different type of university. Over the years, we have grown to become the centre of a vibrant local and global community. Connect with us today . We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index. Explore the fantastic benefits available to you when you become part of the team at Macquarie University. Flexible, hybrid work arrangements 17% Superannuation Subsidised onsite parking options Extensive training and professional development programs Onsite childcare facilities to support working parents Onsite vacation care during school holidays Discounted health insurance Subsidised membership at our Sport & Aquatic Centre Access to an Employee Assistance Program for free and confidential support Convenient onsite GP, imaging, and physiotherapy clinics Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 25/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Finance-Business-Partner_R000024791-1": {
      "title": "Finance Business Partner",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nCompetitive annual package circa $195K (including superannuation) Full-time, continuing contract Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde   Where financial expertise meets strategic impact. About the role   Are you a seasoned finance professional with a passion for driving business success through strategic advice and meaningful financial insights? We're seeking an experienced Finance Business Partner to join our Group Finance team at Macquarie University, where you’ll play a pivotal role in shaping the financial performance and future success of our organisation.   At Macquarie University, we are committed to engaging and empowering the brightest minds to achieve extraordinary outcomes. As a Finance Business Partner, you will work as a trusted advisor, partnering closely with senior stakeholders to provide critical financial insights and drive business decision-making. This is an opportunity to combine your financial expertise with your leadership and strategic capabilities to make a meaningful impact across a diverse and innovative organisation.   The Finance Business Partner works at the intersection of finance and strategy, translating complex data into actionable intelligence that drives business outcomes. This is a high impact role where you will work within the Vice-President Finance and Resources portfolio substantively supporting the property team managing complex physical asset expenditure and budgeting. This position also supports the portfolio of the Vice-President Strategy, Planning and Performance.   What will you do   Partner strategically with key stakeholders to understand their business needs and provide expert financial guidance that influences direction and decision-making. Drive business performance through insightful analysis, scenario modelling, and cost-benefit evaluations that support new initiatives and strategic imperatives. Lead continuous improvement activities within business units, that embed efficient finance processes. Shape financial planning by partnering with business units to develop and critically evaluate annual budgets, forecasts, and long-term financial plans. Deliver high-impact analysis and insights through month-end analyses and management information that tell the story behind the numbers.   About You: (Selection Criteria)   You have experience as a Finance Business Partner managing multiple stakeholders within a large organisation with complex accounting and reporting needs. With sound knowledge of commercial finance and the external finance landscape, you can apply this knowledge to support and influence stakeholders across all levels to ensure delivery. In addition, you will have the following:   Professional credentials – CA/CPA or equivalent qualification. Substantial experience –  At least 4 years post CA/CPA experience in similar roles within large, complex organisations. Business partnering excellence – Proven ability to build rapport and influence senior stakeholders with trust and credibility. Financial Modelling – including scenario analysis and presenting actionable insights to support strategy and decision making. Commercial acumen – Sharp business insight combined with experience applying strong accounting principles. Advanced technical skills – Expertise in financial modelling, scenario analysis, and Microsoft Office (particularly Excel and PowerPoint).   Experience as a Finance Business Partner in the property, construction, or asset management sectors would be highly advantageous.   Why work at Macquarie     Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Celebrating its 60th year in 2024, it was established as a bold experiment in higher education and designed to break from educational traditions to work in tandem with industry. Institutionally we strive for the extraordinary by challenging convention and embracing different views. Our pioneering culture has encouraged and inspired students, staff and collaborators to break free from conventional thinking, and to actively shape the complex issues that define the future of humanity Connect with us today .    We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index, having recently earned a five-star rating in the QS World Rankings with the highest rating for employability. Take a look at the staff benefits on offer.   Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity.  Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for.   Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University.   How to apply   Please apply online and attach your resume and a separate cover letter that outlines how your experience is aligned to the role against the selection criteria.   *Please note this position requires criminal record check.   For a confidential conversation please contact Sarah Bate, Head of Talent Acquisition via sarah.bate@mq.edu.au .   Applications Close:   Tuesday 27 October at 11:59pm AEDT   We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date.  If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 27/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
