    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Lecturer-in-Psychology_R000024915": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Psychology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nSalary Package: Lecturer (Level B) from $127,138 - $150,425 per annum, plus 17% employer's superannuation and annual leave loading Appointment Type: Full time, Continuing Job Family: Balanced (Teaching and Research) Location: Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus Exciting opportunity for a balanced, teaching and research academic to contribute to innovative and impactful teaching and research in Psychology at Macquarie University. The School of Psychological Sciences is seeking a suitably qualified academic to be actively involved in the development, curriculum design, teaching, and delivery of units in the accredited undergraduate and postgraduate psychology courses within the school. The successful candidate will also have a strong track record in research (relative to opportunity), that aligns with the staffs’ strengths within the school. Joining our School at an exciting time of curriculum growth and renewal, you will play a meaningful part in developing and contributing to the teaching of new units, conducting and supervising research and enriching the student experience across one of the largest and most highly regarded psychology suites of courses in the country. The successful applicant will be expected to be available on a full-time basis by January 2027. About the Role As a Lecturer (Level B) you will be involved in unit development and/or re-design, delivery of teaching across our accredited Psychology courses, at both the undergraduate and postgraduate levels. You will also be expected to grow your research track that aligns with the research strengths of staff within the School. Your responsibilities will include: Contributing to unit development and teaching within accredited undergraduate and postgraduate Psychology courses. Delivering and managing teaching content, lectures, tutorials and assessments across face-to-face and/or online modalities. Teaching in applied psychology areas, including psychological assessment, evidenced based therapeutic approaches, and counselling, as well as in social, personality and developmental psychology. Helping to create an engaging and inclusive learning experience for undergraduate and postgraduate cohorts. Conducting impactful research aligned with the School’s strategic priorities, including applying and securing competitive research funding, publishing in Q1-ranked journals, and supervising coursework and higher degree research (HDR) students. Being available on a full-time basis. About Us The School of Psychological Sciences is ranked among the top 75 Psychology Departments in the world and is at the forefront of research, teaching and community engagement. We offer accredited undergraduate and postgraduate programs in Psychology, with the largest suite of postgraduate programs in New South Wales. The school sits within the Faculty of Medicine, Health and Human Sciences (FMHHS), whose education suite includes clinical science, physiotherapy, medicine, exercise and sports science, public health, psychology, cognitive sciences, linguistics, audiology and speech pathology. The faculty forms part of MQ Health, an integrated academic health sciences enterprise incorporating Macquarie University Hospital and primary and speciality clinics. We foster a values-based culture of innovation and creativity to achieve excellence in teaching and to enhance the research performance of the University. We invest in developing the careers and wellbeing of our students and staff, and we live our values of Caring, Integrity, Teamwork, Ambition, Innovation and Engagement. About You You will have a tertiary and professional qualifications in psychology, and the capacity to design, deliver units and programs at both the undergraduate and the postgraduate levels. You will have a strong track record in research that closely aligns with staff’s strengths within the School. You will also have experience with, or a willingness to embrace, educational technology, blended learning and educational innovation. Selection Criteria A PhD or equivalent tertiary qualifications in Psychology. Current registration as a Psychologist (Practicing status) with the Australian Health Practitioner Regulation Agency (AHPRA). Demonstrated ability to deliver high-quality learning and teaching, including the design, delivery, and management of online and face-to-face content, lectures, tutorials, and assessments, with evidence of excellent student outcomes and reflective practice. Demonstrated experience in teaching evidence-based assessment and therapeutic approaches including counselling skills across the lifespan. Demonstrated experience in teaching in one or more of the following areas: social, developmental, personality and health psychology. Demonstrated excellent interpersonal and communication skills, with an ability to relate to build an inclusive teaching and learning environment, and work effectively in a team environment. Evidence of successful delivery to diverse student cohorts and creating a superior student experience characterised by strong engagement at the postgraduate and undergraduate levels. Demonstrated strong track record in research, relative to opportunity, including research grants and peer reviewed publications. Evidence of quality research student supervision (e.g., Honours). Research track that is compatible with the research strengths of staff within the School. How to Apply To be considered, please apply online with your CV and a separate cover letter (3-page maximum) outlining how you meet each of the selection criteria (above). Please note that applications for this position are only being accepted from Australian citizens, permanent residents, and those currently residing in Australia with full working rights. Applications Close : Thursday 5th November at 11.59 PM AEST. Enquiries: For enquiries, or a confidential conversation about the role, please contact Professor Maria Kangas, Head of School of Psychological Sciences at maria.kangas@mq.edu.au . Why Join Us? Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Since our foundation over 60 years ago, we have aspired to be a different type of university. Over the years, we have grown to become the centre of a vibrant local and global community. Connect with us today . We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index, having recently earned a five-star rating in the QS World Rankings with the highest rating for employability. Take a look at the fabulous staff benefits on offer when you work at Macquarie University: Flexible, hybrid work arrangements 17% Superannuation Subsidised onsite parking options Extensive training and professional development programs Onsite childcare facilities to support working parents Onsite vacation care during school holidays Discounted health insurance Subsidised membership at our Sport & Aquatic Centre Access to an Employee Assistance Program for free and confidential support Convenient onsite GP, imaging, and physiotherapy clinics Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 05/11/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Student-and-Education-Digital-Experience-Lead_R000024934": {
      "title": "Student and Education Digital Experience Lead",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nSenior Contract Salary Package 2 Year Fixed-term Contract Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus Lead the digital experience that puts students at the heart of education. Champion innovation across the student journey, bringing together people, technology and insight to create seamless, engaging and inclusive digital experiences that enable students to connect, learn, thrive and succeed. Every student at Macquarie University interacts with our digital services from the moment they apply, through enrolment, learning and all the way to graduation. This newly established role owns the digital experience approach for our student and education domain, supported by a dedicated team, and the development capability focused solely on the student experience. As the Student and Education Digital Experience Lead, you are the primary IT partner, the IT \"front door\" for the Student Services domain. You will work alongside Student Shared Services, Deputy Deans, Faculty Executive Directors, the Dean of Students Office and the PVC Education to connect academic and service priorities with technology capability, so that student needs, service performance, investment decisions and delivery roadmaps stay aligned with the University's strategic objectives. This newly established role is central to Macquarie’s customer-focused, experience-led IT operating model, aligned with IT’s 2027 Workforce Plan and the shift toward domain-focused delivery leadership. It is a high-impact, highly visible position at the intersection of higher education, student services and technology, with the scope, resources and accountability to shape digital experiences for our students. About the Role Reporting to the Chief Information and Digital Officer, you will guide the student and education digital experience end to end. Your focus will include: Developing and maintaining the Student Experience roadmap, domain backlog and prioritisation approach, aligned to business priorities, service outcomes and strategic objectives. Coordinating demand through a single domain view, so work is prioritised and routed appropriately across experience teams, platform teams, project delivery pathways and operational improvement activity. Guiding your team and dedicated development capability to deliver a prioritised backlog of improvements, with attention to backlog health, sequencing, dependencies, delivery predictability and value realisation. Translating student insights, service performance information and journey pain points into prioritised initiatives with measurable outcomes. Partnering with Platform Owners, Architects, and the Cyber, Service Management, Data and AI functions so student experiences make best use of enterprise platforms, reusable capabilities and architectural standards, with security considered from the earliest stages of planning and design. Progressing the responsible adoption of AI-enabled capabilities across the domain, with appropriate governance and oversight. Using customer, service, operational and business data to establish meaningful performance measures, generate actionable insights and monitor digital adoption, product performance and benefits. Reporting domain performance, delivery confidence, adoption, risks, benefits and priorities through Quarterly Business Reviews and other governance forums. Guiding the transition from project-based delivery to enduring product and experience-team ownership, including capability uplift across product, Agile, DevSecOps, analytics, design and change practices. About us Macquarie University Information Technology (MQ IT) embraces the university mission to be bold, distinctive, progressive, and transformational. Information Technology is a trusted business partner with an ethos of service, and we pride ourselves in the application of a strong collaborative partnership approach to transformation across the University. We strive for the efficient provision of services to better support the areas where we should be unique across the education, research, and health portfolios within the University. About You You are an experienced digital, product or service leader with a strong understanding of the higher education sector, university environments and the student experience, with an appreciation of academic and education contexts. You are confident engaging in technical conversations and skilled at building effective relationships across various stakeholders, academic colleagues, platform teams and multidisciplinary teams. Selection Criteria Relevant tertiary qualifications or equivalent professional experience in technology, business, service design, product management, enterprise architecture, transformation, management or a related field. Experience leading student-focused digital experiences within higher education, translating student needs, business priorities and service outcomes into roadmaps, backlogs and continuous improvement initiatives. Well-developed knowledge of student services, and ideally the academic and education domain, including enrolment, learning and teaching, communications and student portals. Demonstrated technical competency with student-facing platforms such as Salesforce CRM, Academic Management Information System (AMIS), MyAcademic and eStudent portals, iLearn Learning Management Systems and Service Connect, with domain-specific understanding. Capability in strategic planning, investment prioritisation, portfolio management and demand management, including balancing competing priorities and making evidence-based decision making. Experience leading or working within Agile, product and DevSecOps environments, embedding continuous improvement, cross-functional collaboration, delivery discipline and secure-by-design practices. Data literacy and evaluative capability, including establishing meaningful performance measures, generating actionable insights and applying them to improve experience and service performance, together with the ability to identify and apply AI and emerging technology opportunities responsibly. Strong leadership, facilitation and communication skills, including guiding multidisciplinary teams, enabling organisational change, building capability, and conveying complex information clearly to executive stakeholders and governance forums. How to Apply To be considered, please apply online with your CV and a cover letter outlining how your experience aligns with the selection criteria (above). Please note work hours may vary from time to time to accommodate business needs Applications Close: 6th November at 11.59 PM AEST. Why Join Us? Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Since our foundation over 60 years ago, we have aspired to be a different type of university. Over the years, we have grown to become the centre of a vibrant local and global community. Connect with us today . We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index. Explore the fantastic benefits available to you when you become part of the team at Macquarie University. Flexible, hybrid work arrangements Subsidised onsite parking options Extensive training and professional development programs Onsite childcare facilities to support working parents Onsite vacation care during school holidays Discounted health insurance Subsidised membership at our Sport & Aquatic Centre Access to an Employee Assistance Program for free and confidential support Convenient onsite GP, imaging, and physiotherapy clinics Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 06/11/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Education-Manager_R000024910": {
      "title": "Education Manager",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nBase salary from $147,124 - $155,386 (HEW Level 9) per annum , plus 17% employer's superannuation and annual leave loading Appointment Type: Full-Time (35 hours per week), fixed-term contract until 23 July 2028 with a possibility of extension Based on site at Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus (North Ryde) About the Role Macquarie University College is seeking to appoint a qualified and highly experienced Education Manager. This is an exciting opportunity for an enthusiastic educational leader to enhance and extend education excellence at Macquarie University College. Key responsibilities of the role, including but not limited to: Managing development, delivery and continuous improvement of Macquarie University College pathway programs and courses. Leading curriculum design, review and innovation, moderation, assessment integrity and educational quality initiatives. Monitoring student progression, retention, success and transition outcomes into undergraduate and postgraduate degrees. Using evidence, data and benchmarking to drive continuous improvement. Developing support strategies for diverse learner cohorts, including domestic and international students. Driving improvements in student engagement, retention and completion rates. Leading teaching staff teams and managing performance, development and workforce planning. Engaging professionally with colleagues and students and contribute to a positive workplace culture. Performing any other duties as required and appropriate for this classification.   About You Macquarie University College provides local and international students with alternative pathway programs to undergraduate and postgraduate degrees through our accelerated face-to-face learning model. The College delivers Foundation & Intensive programs, Diplomas, UniReady and Masters Qualifying programs, English language programs, and operates the Pearson Testing Centre on campus.   About You You are an experienced education leader with a strong track record of managing complex educational programs, leading high-performing teams and delivering outstanding student outcomes. You bring significant experience in higher education, pathway education or student success initiatives, together with the ability to translate strategic priorities into effective operational outcomes. You have demonstrated expertise in academic governance, quality assurance, curriculum development and regulatory compliance, and are confident leading continuous improvement initiatives that enhance student progression, retention and success. You use evidence-based decision making to evaluate performance, identify opportunities and drive innovation across educational programs. A collaborative and influential leader, you build strong relationships with academic and professional staff, senior leaders and external stakeholders. You are skilled at managing change, balancing competing priorities and fostering a culture of excellence, accountability and inclusion. You possess highly developed communication, stakeholder engagement and problem-solving skills, enabling you to provide strategic advice and lead initiatives that support organisational objectives. Experience working with diverse student cohorts, including domestic and international students, is highly regarded. You will hold postgraduate qualifications in education, higher education, management or a related discipline, or an equivalent combination of extensive leadership experience and demonstrated expertise in educational management. Most importantly, you are passionate about creating high-quality learning experiences and supporting students to successfully transition into and thrive within university study.   To Apply To be considered for this position, please apply online and attach your resume and a separate cover letter (no more than 2 pages) that outlines how you meet the selection criteria below: Selection Criteria: Essential Postgraduate qualification in Education, Higher Education, Educational Leadership, Management or a related discipline; OR an equivalent combination of extensive management experience and educational leadership expertise. Significant experience managing courses and programs in a higher education, pathway, VET or similar environment. Demonstrated leadership of multidisciplinary teams. Experience leading curriculum enhancement and quality assurance processes. Highly Desirable Experience in pathway, transition or foundation education. Knowledge of Australian higher education regulation and quality frameworks. Experience managing international student education programs. Experience working within a university governance environment. Senior Fellow (SFHEA) or higher accreditation with AdvanceHE.   * Note: This position is not available for visa sponsorship, and the successful applicant must have valid work rights in Australia. This role requires a National Police Check Clearance and applicants are preferred to hold a current Working with Children Check (WWCC) or be willing to obtain one. Please note that the expectation is that staff will be on campus most workdays.   Specific Role Enquiries: Please contact Akina Banh, Administration Officer ( akina.banh@mq.edu.au ). Application Close: Sunday, 8 November 2026, 23:59pm **** Interviews are expected to be conducted face-to-face on Friday, 20 November 2026. Please ensure you are available on this day. The successful candidate is ideally expected to commence on Monday, 11 January 2027 .   Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 07/11/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
