    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Faculty-Operations-Manager_R000024694": {
      "title": "Faculty Operations Manager",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nFull time\n\nSalary package – from $126,306 per annum (HEW Level 8) plus 17% superannuation and annual leave loading   Appointment type – Full-time continuing    Location - Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde   Shape faculty-wide operations and enable outstanding health education and research   The Faculty of Medicine, Health and Human Sciences (FMHHS) is seeking a Faculty Operations Manager to strengthen how operational and administrative services are planned and delivered across the Faculty. This is an opportunity to shape the priorities, service standards, ways of working and relationships that make operational support genuinely effective.  Working closely with the Head of Faculty Operations and a wide range of stakeholders, you'll sit at the point where strategy becomes day-to-day delivery. From budget planning and resourcing through to staff and student lifecycle administration, you'll make sure the operational foundations are in place so academic colleagues can focus on world-class education, research and clinical activity.  If you enjoy bringing order to complexity, guiding a service-focused team and being the person people turn to for considered advice, this role offers genuine scope to influence outcomes across one of Australia's most ambitious health faculties.  About the Role   As Faculty Operations Manager, you will manage, plan and deliver operational and administrative services across the Faculty, as a key part of its operational services delivery model.  Your responsibilities will include:  Manage the Faculty level Operations team and oversee team performance, professional development and the delivery of high-quality administrative services .  Build and contribute to the development of the annual Faculty budget under the direction of the Head of Faculty Operations and in consultation with the Faculty .  Executive Director and Faculty Finance Business Partner and key stakeholders  In consultation with the Head of Faculty Operations and Finance Business Partner, oversee day-to-day financial operations and budget management.  Manage day-to-day operations at Faculty level, including identifying and resolving operational issues as they arise.  Build and maintain productive stakeholder relationships across the Faculty, MU Health and the wider University , including Property, IT, HR and Finance to ensure strategic and operational activity is coordinated and implemented smoothly.   Represent the Faculty in University-wide strategic initiatives, working with Corporate Shared Services teams and the Operations team to improve service delivery, standardise processes and support improved ways of working.  Support the planning and implementation of Faculty-wide strategic and operational initiatives, coordinating activities across the Faculty and with relevant University teams.  Oversee operational support for Faculty-level teaching units.  In coordination with Faculty Education, Research, Technical and Shared Services, manage the organisation and operational support for staff and students.  Provide high-quality advice to senior Faculty stakeholders, including participation in key committees, preparation of recommendations for Faculty Committee s , and assistance with business plans.    About Us   Macquarie University's Faculty of Medicine, Health and Human Sciences builds on our aspiration to have the nation's first fully integrated Academic Health Sciences Centre under a university's leadership. It brings together the excellent work of medical and allied-health clinicians and researchers across the University and around the country, with unparalleled access to the world-leading clinical resources and research facilities found only on our campus.  Our Faculty Operations team is the engine room behind that ambition - enabling teaching, research and clinical activity through planning, financial stewardship, systems and service excellence, all delivered on a connected campus in North Ryde.  About You   You are an experienced operations or administration professional who is at ease in a complex, people-focused environment. You plan with the long view in mind, yet remain comfortable in the detail — and you bring a calm, service-oriented approach to guiding a team and advising senior stakeholders. Experience in higher education, health or another multifaceted professional setting is highly desired.   Selection Criteria   Relevant tertiary qualification/s and/or equivalent extensive experience  Extensive experience building and guiding high-performing teams to deliver organisational outcomes, including coaching and developing professional staff  Demonstrated ability to plan at both strategic and operational levels, with the organisational skills to manage complex operations, competing priorities and the delivery of programs and services across a diverse portfolio.  Experience working as part of a management team and fostering a cooperative, service-oriented environment, including the capacity to embrace and progress change  Demonstrated experience delivering operational and strategic projects end to end, including scoping, planning, implementation and evaluation, with a proven ability to coordinate delivery across multiple business units.  Well-developed conceptual, evaluative, and problem-solving skills, with the ability to develop practical and innovative solutions  Clear written and verbal communication skills, with a service focus and the ability to work with a diverse range of stakeholders and reach positive negotiated outcomes  Demonstrated ability to manage financial and physical resources, including budget development and day-to-day financial oversight; experience in a higher education and/or healthcare environment will be well regarded  How to Apply   To be considered, please apply online with your CV and a cover letter outlining how your experience aligns with the selection criteria (above).   Applications Close: Thursday 5th November, 11:59pm AEST    For role-specific enquires, please reach out to Sarah Furlong, Head of Faculty Operations at sarah.furlong@mq.edu.au  For general enquires, reach out to Rebecca Wood, Talent Acquisition at r.wood@mq.edu.au    We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date.   **Please note this position is only open to Australian citizens, permanent residents and those currently residing in Australia with full working rights**   Pre-Employment Checks   Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for.  Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 05/11/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Data-Analysis-Officer_R000024923": {
      "title": "Data Analysis Officer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nFull time\n\n$102,136 – 112,741 per annum (HEW Level 6), plus 17% employer's superannuation and annual leave loading Full-time, 16-month fixed-term contract Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus Data tells a story, and at Macquarie University, that story informs how we invest in research, how we measure our performance, and how we present ourselves on the world stage. We're hiring for a Data Analysis Officer to join our Business Intelligence and Reporting (BIR) team, where your analysis will directly inform decisions made at the highest levels of the University. Sitting within the Vice-President, Strategy, Planning and Performance (VPSPP) portfolio, BIR enables evidence-based decision-making across the institution. In this role, you'll work alongside the Lead Data Analyst and a skilled team of analysts, data engineers and IT specialists to deliver enterprise analytics and reporting that supports research performance, return on research investment, and rankings submissions. You'll also contribute to Digital Transformation projects that are modernising how the University uses its data. This is a genuinely visible role for someone who enjoys the full breadth of analytics work such as improving data quality, building reporting solutions, and translating technical findings into plain-language insight for senior stakeholders. About the Role Reporting to the Lead Data Analyst, you will: Support the Lead Data Analyst in the development and delivery of enterprise analytics and reporting solutions, as part of both business-as-usual work and Digital Transformation projects. Review and analyse databases and systems to ensure data is accessible and can be meaningfully collated, producing accurate insights and information for clients and stakeholders. Assess data sources to identify gaps and verify accuracy and consistency. Provide advice and guidance to clients on relevant analytics platforms and technologies, including identifying and resolving issues to improve efficiency and effectiveness. Contribute to the design, implementation and operation of analytics platforms and technologies, liaising with internal and external stakeholders, service partners and suppliers, and ensuring compliance with Macquarie University and MQ IT standards and processes. Monitor, analyse and report on the availability, performance and capacity of services and resources, assess new initiatives and make recommendations to improve service delivery. Liaise with rankings and research data providers to deliver research and rankings submissions. Contribute to continuous improvement of processes, standards and procedures, and maintain support documentation so tasks are performed reliably and consistently. Help build data analytics capability across the University and contribute to knowledge sharing.   About Us The Vice-President, Strategy, Planning and Performance portfolio holds executive responsibility for the development and execution of University strategy, cross-institutional planning, and oversight of whole-of-Group performance. The portfolio assists the Vice-Chancellor, Executive Group and University Council in sustaining the long-term direction of the University and its subsidiaries, with accountabilities spanning institutional strategy, transformational change, continuous improvement, performance metrics and reporting frameworks. Business Intelligence and Reporting (BIR) sits at the centre of this work, enabling evidence-based decision-making across the University. About You You are a capable analyst who enjoys working with data end-to-end, from questioning the source to presenting the insight. You're comfortable in a multi-stakeholder environment, you communicate technical information clearly to non-technical audiences, and you take pride in work that is accurate, well-documented and delivered on time. Selection Criteria Tertiary qualifications in a related field and/or equivalent knowledge, skills and experience. Working knowledge of one or more of the following: Alteryx, SQL, AWS, Power BI/Tableau, and proficiency with the Microsoft Office suite. Experience assisting the development and delivery of data analytics solutions within complex, multi-stakeholder environments. Demonstrated experience performing analysis using a variety of methods across both relational and non-relational data sets to enable evidence-based decision-making. Well-developed analytical and problem-solving skills, including the ability to interpret requirements and information drawn from numerous sources. Effective communication skills, with the ability to establish and maintain productive working relationships with internal and external stakeholders. Sound organisational and time management skills, including experience working to deadlines and documenting operational support procedures. How to Apply To be considered, please apply online with your CV and a cover letter outlining how your experience aligns with the selection criteria (above). Kindly please note that we are only accepting applications from Australian citizens, permanent residents, and individuals residing in Australia who hold full working rights. Applications Close Date : 1st November at 11.59 PM AEST. Why Join Us? Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Since our foundation over 60 years ago, we have aspired to be a different type of university. Over the years, we have grown to become the centre of a vibrant local and global community. Connect with us today .   We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index, having recently earned a five-star rating in the QS World Rankings with the highest rating for employability. Take a look at the fabulous staff benefits on offer when you work at Macquarie University: Flexible, hybrid work arrangements 17% Superannuation Subsidised onsite parking options Extensive training and professional development programs Onsite childcare facilities to support working parents Onsite vacation care during school holidays Discounted health insurance Subsidised membership at our Sport & Aquatic Centre Access to an Employee Assistance Program for free and confidential support Convenient onsite GP, imaging, and physiotherapy clinics Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 01/11/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/ARC-Postdoctoral-Research-Fellow--Philosophy-of-Biology-_R000024560": {
      "title": "ARC Postdoctoral Research Fellow (Philosophy of Biology)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nFull time\n\n· Annual Salary Package: From $127,138 (Level B.1), plus 17% employer's superannuation and annual leave loading. · Appointment type: Full-time, 3-year fixed term contract · Location: Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde About the Role This position is part of ARC Discovery Project “Health, Biological Fitness and Environmental Diversity”. The appointee will work with Dr Bourrat (Macquarie University, Philosophy), Professor Raubenheimer (University of Sydney, Charles Perkins Centre), Emeritus Professor Griffiths (University of Sydney & Macquarie University, Philosophy), and collaborators to develop a framework for understanding how the organism–environment interface shapes biological fitness, adaptation, and health. The successful candidate will contribute to all aspects of the project in collaboration with the research team. This will include: 1. Developing an integrative framework for different measures of biological fitness. 2. Developing a framework for understanding the role of the environment in explanations of adaptation. 3. Exploring the implications of these frameworks for understanding health. The research will involve close collaboration between philosophy and biological sciences and requires expertise at the intersection of philosophy of biology and evolutionary biology. The position will be based in the Theory and Methods in Bioscience group, led by Dr Bourrat within the Philosophy Discipline, and will also be affiliated with the University of Sydney’s Charles Perkins Centre. About Us Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Since our foundation in 1964, we have aspired to be a different type of university. Over the years, we've grown to become the centre of a vibrant local and global community. Connect with us today .  Within the University, the Faculty of Arts is one of Australia’s leading arts and humanities faculties, bringing together a diverse community of educators, researchers and professional staff. Its professional staff work in partnership with academic colleagues to support the faculty’s teaching, research and engagement through high-quality administrative services.   The position is based in the School of Humanities within the Faculty of Arts. For further information on the research activities of the team, please visit the following websites: Dr Pierrick Bourrat: https://pierrickbourrat.com/ Prof. David Raubenheimer: https://profiles.sydney.edu.au/david.raubenheimer Emer. Prof. Paul Griffiths: https://tmbiosci.org/person/?personId=90 How to Apply Please apply online and attach your resume (including a list of two referees), and a separate cover letter that outlines how you meet the selection criteria below. Referees should not send reference letters unless contacted directly by Macquarie University. The University will contact referees, if reference checks are required at a later stage of the selection process. Essential Selection Criteria: PhD in Philosophy (awarded) or another field relevant to the research project, Demonstrated expertise in Philosophy of Biology and/or Theoretical Biology, with a specific focus on evolutionary biology, A strong track record of publications in high-quality, peer-reviewed journals at the intersection of philosophy of biology and evolutionary biology, Proven ability to conduct highly interdisciplinary research, bridging philosophical theory with empirical findings from the biological sciences, and Excellent communication and collaboration skills, with evidence of ability to work effectively within an interdisciplinary research team and to meet project deadlines. Note: Please note this position requires a criminal history/ police check and an academic qualification check. *** International applicants are welcome to apply. For specific role enquires, please contact Pierrick Bourrat, Senior Lecturer at pierrick.bourrat@mq.edu.au Applications Close: Sunday 22 November at 11:59 p.m. (AEST) *** We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date. Why Join Us? We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index, having recently earned a five-star rating in the QS World Rankings with the highest rating for employability. Our prime location is just a short walk from Macquarie University Metro Station and Macquarie Shopping Centre. Enjoy the benefits of working at a campus that offers: 17% Superannuation Subsidised onsite parking options Flexible working options Training and professional development Onsite childcare facilities Discounted health insurance (Medibank) Onsite vacation care Employee Assistance Program Subsidised membership at the Sport & Aquatic Centre Onsite GP, imaging & physio clinics Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 21/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Senior-Lecturer-in-Natural-Sciences--Teaching-and-Leadership-_R000024434": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer in Natural Sciences (Teaching and Leadership)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nFull time\n\n- Salary package: $$155,236 - $164,549 (Level C.1- C.3) plus 17% employer's superannuation contribution and annual leave loading. - Full-time, continuing role - Based at Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde The Role We are seeking a highly motivated and skilled Teaching and Leadership academic to lead and contribute to teaching, curriculum development, and governance within the School of Natural Sciences. This is a strategic academic leadership role for an outstanding educator with expertise in teaching governance, curriculum leadership, and academic quality. The successful candidate will provide leadership across undergraduate and postgraduate education in conservation , climate change and ecology , driving excellence in curriculum design, pedagogical innovation, and course planning. They will play a central role in academic governance, leading curriculum review, accreditation, quality assurance, and continuous improvement processes to ensure programs remain academically rigorous, compliant, and responsive to evolving student and industry needs. The role also requires demonstrated experience in leading, mentoring, and developing academic teaching teams, fostering a culture of educational excellence, collaboration, and evidence-informed practice across the School. Essential selection criteria Demonstrated experience in curriculum design, review and innovation , with evidence of developing and delivering high-quality curricula aligned with institutional strategy and pedagogical practice. Demonstrated experience in course and program-level development , including curriculum planning, quality assurance, assessment and continuous improvement, with the capacity to contribute to accreditation and academic governance processes. Experience in fostering a positive learning and teaching culture , including supporting and mentoring academic and sessional teaching staff. Demonstrated commitment to inclusive, student-centred and experiential learning , with evidence of approaches that enhance student engagement, learning outcomes and the student experience. Demonstrated leadership in education governance and strategic initiatives through participation in School, Faculty and/or University committees, working groups or equivalent activities. Evidence of disciplinary scholarship and professional engagement , with the capacity to develop productive relationships with industry, professional bodies and/or other external stakeholders relevant to education and the discipline. Demonstrated high-level communication, collaboration and interpersonal skills , including the ability to work collegially with diverse stakeholders and represent the School effectively within the University and externally. Demonstrated experience in strategic teaching and resource planning , including the equitable allocation of teaching workloads, alignment of teaching responsibilities with staff expertise, and delivery of curriculum within workload and budget parameters. About You You are an experienced and collaborative academic with a strong record of leadership in teaching, curriculum design, and academic governance. You bring demonstrated expertise in course planning, quality assurance, and program-level curriculum reform, along with the ability to mentor and support academic and sessional teaching staff. With excellent organisational and communication skills, you lead and contribute positively to School and Faculty committees, workload planning, and learning and teaching culture, while maintaining active engagement in disciplinary scholarship and external partnerships to enhance student learning and education impact. About Us The School of Natural Sciences is a multidisciplinary and collegial environment committed to excellence in teaching, research, and student experience. We deliver innovative, research-led education across biological, environmental, physical and molecular sciences, and value collaboration, curiosity, and impact in everything we do. To Apply To apply for this position, please apply online by submitting your CV and a separate cover letter (no more than 2 pages) that demonstrates how you meet the following selection criteria: PhD in conservation, ecology, or a closely related discipline (or near completion). Demonstrated strong teaching experience in undergraduate and postgraduate biology, ecology, conservation and climate change. Evidence of leadership in curriculum and unit design, renewal, and teaching innovation. Strong experience in course planning, academic governance, and quality assurance processes, including assessment design and moderation. Evidence of leadership, team management, and collaboration skills, including the ability to coordinate teaching teams, mentor academic and sessional staff, and contribute effectively to committees. Role-specific Enquiries: Associate Professor Fleur Ponton, Head of School fleur.ponton@mq.edu.au . Applications Close: Wednesday November 18th 2026 at 11:59pm (AEDT) Please note that applications for this position are only being accepted from Australian citizens, permanent residents, and those currently residing in Australia with full working rights. ** Applications will be reviewed as they are received, and we reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date. We also reserve the right to close the advertisement early if a sufficient number of qualified applicants is received. The Faculty of Science and Engineering at Macquarie University has a goal to increase the engagement of women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people from diverse backgrounds in STEMM roles. Applications are considered holistically, and candidates are encouraged to apply even if their experience does not meet each individual selection criterion.​ Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 18/11/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/CAD-Co-ordinator_R000024761": {
      "title": "CAD Co-ordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nFull time\n\n$107,022 per annum (HEW Level 6), plus 17% employer's superannuation and annual leave loading Full-time, continuing Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus An exciting opportunity for an experienced CAD Co-ordinator to work in a high performing team environment . Every new building, refurbishment and transformed learning space at Macquarie University starts with accurate, reliable data. As our CAD Coordinator, you’ll play a key role in maintaining the digital information and technical systems that support the University’s built environment, enabling informed decisions across space planning, asset management and project design and delivery. This is an exciting opportunity within our Property Division, with a newly reclassified role that reflects the growing technical expertise required across CAD, BIM/Revit and Archibus. You’ll have the opportunity to make a real impact by strengthening CAD standards and governance, improving processes, and contributing to automation and system integration initiatives across these platforms. Working collaboratively with our Strategy & Planning and Project Management teams, as well as a broad range of internal and external stakeholders, consultants and contractors, you’ll help ensure our property data is accurate, consistent and fit for purpose. If you’re passionate about technical precision, digital innovation and improving the way information supports the built environment, this is your opportunity to shape the systems and standards behind the spaces where our university community learns, works and connects. About the Role Reporting to the Space Planning Data Manager, you will manage and develop the University's CAD database, Archibus system and BIM/Revit models, ensuring data integrity, system quality and accessible, accurate drawing and asset information. Your key accountabilities will include: Enabling space management and planning activity, including transmittal of BIM and CAD documentation for projects and planning (such as the Master Planning Campus Model), drafting CAD concept plans, sketches and diagrams, and contributing to space audits and furniture mapping across our Capus. Coordinating and administering 'as-built' CAD documentation received from consultant teams and contractors for inclusion in the University drawing database using AutoCAD (Autodesk). Maintaining all drawings within the CAD database to current naming and layering conventions and owning CAD standards governance including drawing quality reviews and audits. Managing the Archibus system, including data integrity, drawing integration and system quality assurance, and identifying, troubleshooting and resolving system issues or escalating where appropriate. Maintaining, reviewing and coordinating BIM and Revit models that inform planning, project delivery and asset management outcomes. Leading the development, implementation and monitoring of CAD design standards and procedures to meet customer requirements and industry benchmarks for continuous improvement. Developing and maintaining a central drawing database for authorised user access and assisting the wider Property Division with drawing and documentation requirements. Contributing to automation, process improvement and integration initiatives across the CAD, BIM and Archibus platforms, and providing ongoing and ad-hoc reporting and data visualisation of space utilisation. About Us The Property Division assists the University in achieving its learning, teaching and research goals through planning, development and maintenance services for all University buildings and infrastructure, as well as managing a growing commercial property investment portfolio. Please note that work hours may vary from time to time to accommodate business needs. Macquarie University is a place of inspiration, a university known for its research excellence, progressive teaching and a campus set within 126 hectares of parkland. Our Property Division plays a defining part in that experience, planning and caring for the academic, research and commercial precincts that bring our community of students, researchers, clinicians and professional staff into one connected place. Here, technical expertise is valued, questions are welcomed, and good ideas are given room to grow. About You You are a CAD and BIM specialist who takes pride in accuracy, consistency and well-governed data. You enjoy being the person others rely on for the correct drawing, and you look for better ways to organise, automate and present information. You work comfortably with consultants and contractors, translate their documentation into university protocols, and explain technical detail in plain language to non-technical colleagues. Selection Criteria A degree in a field related to architecture, construction or engineering, or an equivalent combination of relevant experience and/or education and training. Extensive knowledge of computer-aided design (CAD) and Building Information Modelling (BIM) systems and software, including hands-on experience with AutoCAD (Autodesk) and Revit (Autodesk). Demonstrated experience administering and maintaining a CAD library and central drawing database, including data integrity and system quality assurance. Experience administering Archibus or an equivalent IWMS/space management platform, including troubleshooting and progressing system enhancements. Demonstrated ability to modify CAD drawing material provided by external consultants so that it complies with organisational protocols and standards. Well-developed written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to prepare clear, accurate written material and to build effective working relationships with internal and external stakeholders. Demonstrated ability to manage your own workload with minimal day-to-day direction within a multi-disciplinary team environment, and to keep pace with industry trends and developments in the CAD field. Experience in the higher education sector is desirable, though not essential. How to Apply To be considered, please apply online with your CV and a cover letter outlining how your experience aligns with the selection criteria (above). Kindly please note that we are only accepting applications from Australian citizens, permanent residents, and individuals residing in Australia who hold full working rights. Applications Close Date : Tuesday 3rd November at 11.59 PM AEST. Why Join Us? Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Since our foundation over 60 years ago, we have aspired to be a different type of university. Over the years, we have grown to become the centre of a vibrant local and global community. Connect with us today . We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index, having recently earned a five-star rating in the QS World Rankings with the highest rating for employability. Take a look at the fabulous staff benefits on offer when you work at Macquarie University: Flexible, hybrid work arrangements 17% Superannuation Subsidised onsite parking options Extensive training and professional development programs Onsite childcare facilities to support working parents Onsite vacation care during school holidays Discounted health insurance Subsidised membership at our Sport & Aquatic Centre Access to an Employee Assistance Program for free and confidential support Convenient onsite GP, imaging, and physiotherapy clinics Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 03/11/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Lecturer-Senior-Lecturer--Psychology-_R000024853-1": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (Psychology)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\nFull time\n\nSalary Package: Lecturer (Level B) from $127,138 to $150,425 per annum or Senior Lecturer (Level C) from $155,236 to $178,523 plus 17% employer's superannuation and annual leave loading Appointment Type: Continuing, Full-time Location: Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde Exciting opportunity for a Teaching and Leadership academic to contribute to innovative and impactful teaching and leadership in Psychology at Macquarie University, with particular contributions to Clinical Neuropsychology and Applied Psychology training. The School of Psychological Sciences, within the Faculty of Medicine, Health and Human Sciences (FMHHS) is seeking a suitably qualified academic to be actively involved in the development, curriculum design, teaching and delivery of units as well as supervision in the accredited Master of Clinical Neuropsychology postgraduate psychology course, the Master of Professional Psychology and the Undergraduate Psychology Courses within the School. Joining our School at an exciting time of curriculum growth and renewal, you will play a meaningful part in developing new units and enriching the student experience across one of the largest and most highly regarded psychology courses in the country. If you are passionate about teaching and supervising in applied psychology and neuropsychology, helping students build the skills that shape professional practice, we would be glad to hear from you. The successful applicant will be expected to be available on a full-time basis by January 2027. About the Role As a Lecturer (Level B) or Senior Lecturer (Level C) you will be involved in unit development and/or re-design, delivery of teaching across our accredited Psychology courses, as well as supervising students in the Master of Clinical Neuropsychology and the Master of Professional Psychology. Your responsibilities will include: Contributing to unit development and teaching within accredited undergraduate and postgraduate Psychology courses including the Master of Neuropsychology. Delivering and managing teaching content, lectures, tutorials and assessments across face-to-face and/or online modalities. Teaching in applied psychology areas, including clinical neuropsychology, psychological assessment, neuropsychological rehabilitation, counselling and/or therapeutic skills, and developmental psychology. Helping to create an engaging and inclusive learning experience for undergraduate and postgraduate cohorts. About Us The School of Psychological Sciences is ranked among the top 75 Psychology Departments in the world and is at the forefront of research, teaching and community engagement. We offer accredited undergraduate and postgraduate programs in Psychology, with the largest suite of postgraduate programs in New South Wales. The school sits within the Faculty of Medicine, Health and Human Sciences (FMHHS), whose education suite includes clinical science, physiotherapy, medicine, exercise and sports science, public health, psychology, cognitive sciences, linguistics, audiology and speech pathology. The faculty forms part of MQ Health, an integrated academic health sciences enterprise incorporating Macquarie University Hospital and primary and speciality clinics. We foster a values-based culture of innovation and creativity to achieve excellence in teaching and to enhance the research performance of the University. We invest in developing the careers and wellbeing of our students and staff, and we live our values of Caring, Integrity, Teamwork, Ambition, Innovation and Engagement. About You You will have a tertiary and professional qualifications in neuropsychology, and the capacity to design, deliver units and programs at both the undergraduate and the postgraduate levels. You will also have experience with, or a willingness to embrace, educational technology, blended learning and educational innovation. Essential Criteria for Level B (Lecturer) and Level C (Senior Lecturer) A PhD or equivalent tertiary qualifications in Psychology. Current registration as a Psychologist (Practicing status) with the Australian Health Practitioner Regulation Agency (AHPRA). Current endorsement as a Clinical Neuropsychologist with AHPRA (and with minimum 18 months with full endorsement status). Demonstrated ability to deliver high-quality learning and teaching, including the design, delivery, and management of online and face-to-face content, lectures, tutorials, and assessments, with evidence of excellent student outcomes and reflective practice. Demonstrated experience in and/or with the teaching of major methods of evidence-based psychological and neuropsychological assessment, such as the Wechsler tests, personality inventories, and measures of general psychological distress and functioning across the lifespan. Demonstrated experience in teaching evidence-based therapeutic approaches and counselling skills across the lifespan. Demonstrated excellent interpersonal and communication skills, with an ability to relate to build an inclusive teaching and learning environment, and work effectively in a team environment. Evidence of successful delivery to diverse student cohorts and creating a superior student experience characterised by strong engagement at the postgraduate and undergraduate levels. Evidence of quality coursework research supervision (e.g., Honours). Essential for Level C (Senior Lecturer) Demonstrated leadership experience in the delivery of units and programs, working collaboratively with other academics and colleagues, and remaining up to date with developments in the field including evidence-based assessment and therapeutic practices. Outstanding and sustained learning and teaching experience with demonstrated experience of involvement in course/curriculum development. Ability to proactively engage or partner with industry and professional bodies on relevant projects and to represent the School to external stakeholders and the general public. Demonstrated experience to make a contribution to the academic life and administrative tasks of the School and Faculty along with a track record of effective teamwork. How to Apply To be considered, please apply online with your CV and a separate cover letter (3-page maximum) outlining how you meet each of the selection criteria (above). Please note that applications for this position are only being accepted from Australian citizens, permanent residents, and those currently residing in Australia with full working rights. Applications Close : Tuesday 3rd November at 11.59 PM AEST. Enquiries: For enquiries, or a confidential conversation about the role, please contact Professor Maria Kangas, Head of School of Psychological Sciences at maria.kangas@mq.edu.au . Why Join Us? Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Since our foundation over 60 years ago, we have aspired to be a different type of university. Over the years, we have grown to become the centre of a vibrant local and global community. Connect with us today . We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index, having recently earned a five-star rating in the QS World Rankings with the highest rating for employability. Take a look at the fabulous staff benefits on offer when you work at Macquarie University: Flexible, hybrid work arrangements 17% Superannuation Subsidised onsite parking options Extensive training and professional development programs Onsite childcare facilities to support working parents Onsite vacation care during school holidays Discounted health insurance Subsidised membership at our Sport & Aquatic Centre Access to an Employee Assistance Program for free and confidential support Convenient onsite GP, imaging, and physiotherapy clinics Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 03/11/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Expression-of-Interest---Teaching-Associate--School-of-Engineering---Session-1-2027_R000024768": {
      "title": "Expression of Interest – Teaching Associate, School of Engineering - Session 1 2027",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\nPart time\n\nDISCOVER, CREATE, INNOVATE  The Faculty of Science and Engineering at Macquarie University delivers quality education to enable our students to reach their full potential, and work with our communities to discover, create and innovate with sustainability at our core.  THE ROLE  The School of Engineering is inviting expressions of interest for inclusion within our casual academic pool for 2027.   For your application to be considered for Session 1 2027, please register your Expression of Interest (EOI) by Friday 27 November by uploading your relevant qualifications and requested details via the Workday application process. The School of Engineering offers a range of undergraduate and postgraduate units to students completing courses in the Faculty of Science and Engineering. We employ casual academic staff to support our teaching of these courses.   We are currently inviting Expressions of interest (EOIs) from appropriately qualified individuals who demonstrate the following skills, qualifications, and experience.   ESSENTIAL CRITERIA   Completed Bachelor and/or Master’s degree in Engineering, or a closely related discipline.  Hands-on experience in applying theoretical knowledge to real-world problems and projects. An understanding and appreciation of scholarly teaching, particularly project-based learning. Excellent communication skills and proactive student engagement. Proven ability to interact effectively with students, staff and the community.   TO APPLY  All interested applicants are required to upload a copy of their CV , copy of degree / testamur and a cover letter addressing the above criteria as part of the EOI process.  To assist in the review process, please complete this survey Qualtrics Survey | Qualtrics Experience Management (this survey is compulsory)   If you are already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health): Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs.  If you are NOT currently part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health): click the 'Apply' button.    *Please note that this position is not available for visa sponsorship and the successful applicant must have work rights in Australia*   Position Enquiries: Elizabeth Bignucolo, Sessional Academic Staff Coordinator at elizabeth.bignucolo@mq.edu.au . We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 27/11/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Learning-Advisor-Academic-Success-Officer_R000024096": {
      "title": "Learning Advisor/Academic Success Officer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-28\nFull time\n\nSalary Package: Annual base from $114,992 - $124,676 per annum (HEW 7), plus 17% employer's superannuation and annual leave loading Appointment Type: Full-time, continuing Location: Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, Dharug land, North Ryde Macquarie University is recruiting an Academic Success Officer (Learning Advisor) to join the dynamic Academic Success team within the Office of the Pro-Vice Chancellor, Education. Academic Success Officers design and deliver academic, digital, and professional literacies initiatives to maximise student success. This professional position includes delivering student-facing concurrent support initiatives, especially to those identified as being most at risk, supporting peer-led support activities, and designing and delivering impactful integrated or embedded workshops for students and/or staff. You are committed to research-informed design and best practice in inclusive program delivery. High-level analytical and problem-solving skills, including the ability to think strategically and creatively, allow you to respond to student needs and institutional priorities. Equally, your positive and flexible approach to unexpected or changing circumstances enables you to support both colleagues and stakeholders thoughtfully and effectively. If you are energised by the opportunity to transform coursework students’ learning experience, this is a role in which you will thrive.  About Us The Deputy Vice-Chancellor (Academic) is the Chief Academic Officer of the University and is the member of the University Executive with overall responsibility for the planning, quality and delivery of education provided to Macquarie's undergraduate and graduate students. The Pro Vice-Chancellor (Education) is responsible for the University’s educational endeavour across all aspects of the educational lifecycle, including pathways and access, curriculum and educational capability development, educational outcomes and graduate success.  The PVCE provides leadership in the development and implementation of strategies and programs to support the University’s education mission. The Academic Success team within this portfolio is responsible for the student-facing and staff-facing support to coursework students across the University. To Apply  To be considered for this position, please apply online and attach your resume and a separate cover letter that outlines how you meet to the selection criteria below: Postgraduate qualification in education, teaching, or an academic literacies-related field. Sustained relevant experience working with domestic and international students individually and in groups to support the development of academic and/or digital literacies and to maximise academic success at university. Demonstrated capability in the end-to-end design and delivery of curricular and co-curricular initiatives in partnership with academics and other stakeholders.  Knowledge of the higher education sector and literature, including legislative and regulatory requirements relating to academic success and support for students.  Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Demonstrated capability to work productively with stakeholders in an exemplary professional, collaborative, and innovative team environment.  *Work hours may vary from time to time to accommodate business needs. As this is a student-facing role; it is expected that you will be available to work on campus most days of the week. This role requires a National Police Check Clearance and applicants are preferred to hold a current Working with Children Check (WWCC) or be willing to obtain one. ****Please note: This position is not available for visa sponsorship, and the successful applicant must have valid work rights in Australia.*** Specific Role Inquiries: Akina Banh, Administration Officer, akina.banh@mq.edu.au Application Close: Sunday, 15 November 2026, 23:59pm Please note that interviews are expected to be conducted face-to-face on Friday, 27 November 2026. Kindly ensure you are available on this day.   Why work at Macquarie?  Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Since our foundation over 60 years ago, we have aspired to be a different type of university. Over the years, we have grown to become the centre of a vibrant local and global community. Connect with us today . We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index. Explore the fantastic benefits available to you when you become part of the team at Macquarie University. 17% Superannuation   Subsidised onsite parking options  Flexible working options  Training and professional development  Onsite childcare facilities  Discounted health insurance (Medibank)  Onsite vacation care  Employee Assistance Program  Subsidised membership at the Sport & Aquatic Centre Onsite GP, imaging & physio clinics Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 15/11/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    }
  },
